<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Norba</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Latium</i>,
			now called <i>Norma</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
			34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Norbānus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Norba, Norban</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
					19</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Norbāni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				Norbans</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 8, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 64</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Norbānus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a Roman surname in
				the</i> gens Vibia: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">C. Norbanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 2, 21, 89</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
